{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>To your seed I have given.</b> The utterance of the Holy One, blessed be He, is as though it were already done." "<b>The great river.</b> Because it is attached to the land of Israel, He calls it 'great,' even though it is last among the four rivers that go out from Eden, as it says ״וְהַנָּהָר הָרְבִיעִי הוּא פְרָת.״ A parable of a layman: a servant of the king — the king attaches him to the king and they bow to you (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:51.676264754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}